MtCache is a multi-tiered (DRAM / PMEM / SSD) cache engine. It is vendored into
the TemporalStore repository as a dependency and originated from an internal
multi-tiered cache codebase; the version published here has been prepared for
open-source distribution.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The build fetches and links a number of third-party libraries. Each remains
under its own license; this NOTICE does not relicense them. Declarations live
under `third_party/externals/`.

Apache-2.0 or permissive (MIT/BSD/ISC/zlib) licensed dependencies include:
  Abseil, Boost, Folly, fmt, gflags, glog, GoogleTest, jemalloc, libaio,
  libevent, libmemcached, libsodium, libunwind, lz4, xz/lzma, snappy,
  double-conversion, xxHash, zlib, zstd, OpenSSL.

Internal / not-yet-open dependencies (see docs/mtcache_open_source_readiness.md):
  - bytedisk  — distributed only as an internal prebuilt binary; no public
                source. Required only for certain SSD/PMEM storage paths.
  - noodle    — internal metrics/concurrency library; the metrics reporting
                headers are used by the SSD and zoned-store engines.

These internal dependencies are the primary blockers to a fully self-contained
open-source build and are tracked in the readiness document above.
